body: |-
  ## Vision Pivot

  The original Canvas spec (docs/specs/canvas.md) described a tldraw-based symbol visualization canvas — showing Paradigm symbols as cards on an infinite canvas. During planning, the user clarified their actual goal: a free, open-source visual design tool (like Penpot/Figma) where UI elements are Paradigm-native, designs output real CSS, and Claude can see/modify designs via conversation.

  ## Key Decisions

  1. **Craft.js over tldraw** — tldraw is great for diagrams but fights you on precise CSS layout. Craft.js renders actual DOM with actual CSS — what you see IS the CSS. MIT license, ~40KB gzipped.

  2. **Craft.js over GrapesJS** — User chose maximum control. Craft.js gives us the editor framework (drag-drop, component tree, serialization, selection) while we build all UI ourselves.

  3. **Structured layout (flexbox/grid)** — Not absolute positioning. Elements flow with real CSS layout, producing production-ready CSS output.

  4. ***.canvas files as first-class project objects** — Not hidden in .paradigm/canvas/. YAML format, project root default, discovered by glob, git-tracked. This makes canvas files committable project artifacts.

  5. **Graph coexists** — Graph stays as the quick topology view, Canvas is the persistent design editor. Different tools for different jobs.

  ## What Was Built (Sprint 0)

  ### Backend
  - Express router with 4 endpoints: glob discovery, YAML read, YAML write, delete
  - 5-second TTL cache on file discovery, path traversal protection
  - Mounted at /api/canvas/files/* in platform-server

  ### Frontend (25 new files)
  - 5 user components: Container (flexbox, accepts children), Text (inline editable), Button, Image (with placeholder), Spacer
  - 3 editor core components: CanvasEditor (Craft.js wrapper), CanvasFrame (white design surface), RenderNode (selection/hover outlines)
  - 8 panel components: ComponentPalette (left, 200px), PropertyPanel (right, 280px), 6 sub-panels (Layout, Spacing, Size, Typography, Background, Border)
  - Toolbar: file picker, new/save/delete, undo/redo, design/preview toggle
  - Zustand store: file CRUD, debounced auto-save, localStorage last-opened
  - Canvas serializer (Craft.js JSON ↔ YAML), CSS serializer stub
  - Sync hook (editor state ↔ store bidirectional)

  ### Paradigm Compliance
  - .purpose file with 15 components, 3 flows, 3 gates, 6 signals, 4 aspects
  - Routes .purpose updated with CanvasRouter
  - Index rebuilt

  ## Sprint Roadmap

  - S1: Full CSS + responsive breakpoints + layers panel + CSS output view
  - S2: Reusable components + Paradigm #symbol linking
  - S3: MCP tools + CLI + AI integration (Claude can modify designs)
  - S4: Bidirectional CSS sync (design ↔ source code)
  - S5: Export, templates, polish
